warning
# Issue #1933: the batched GraphQL issue-state query (are_issues_open)
# partially failed -- a per-node `Could not resolve` error left some issue
# numbers unresolved, and the parallel per-issue `issue_view` fallback ran
# for exactly those numbers instead of the whole batch. Warning, not error:
# the call still completes correctly, but a high rate means stale issue
# references are degrading `fleet status --json`'s fast path. The payload
# names the unresolved numbers (the telemetry the incident lacked).
# Edge-triggered (rework review): `are_issues_open` emits this once per
# newly-unresolved issue number per GitHub-instance lifetime. The emitter
# tracks numbers already reported; a number leaves the tracked set only
# when a later batch positively resolves it, so a persistent stale blocker
# produces one row rather than one per loop pass -- the every-pass warning
# flood shape #1271/#1768 already burned once for check_warning_events --
# while a number that resolves and later goes stale again fires a fresh
# warning. Short-lived processes such as `fleet status --json` still emit
# once per invocation: their GitHub instance does not outlive the run, so
# there is nothing to dedupe against.
